    {
      "id": "punctuation",
      "title": "Punctuation",
      "fr": "la ponctuation",
      "level": "A1",
      "keywords": [
        "punctuation",
        "space before question mark",
        "? ! : ;",
        "guillemets",
        "quotation marks",
        "« »",
        "comma",
        "ponctuation"
      ],
      "topics": [],
      "see": [
        "conjunctions",
        "complex-sentences"
      ],
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "In short",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "In French a **space** is written before the two-part marks *? ! : ;* and inside quotation marks « ». English does not do this."
            },
            {
              "type": "compare",
              "items": [
                {
                  "en": "How are you?",
                  "fr": "Ça va[[ ]]?"
                },
                {
                  "en": "Watch out!",
                  "fr": "Attention[[ ]]!"
                },
                {
                  "en": "He said: \"Hi.\"",
                  "fr": "Il a dit[[ ]]: « Salut. »"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Quotation marks",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "French quotation marks look like arrows « ... » (*les guillemets*) and have a space inside. In dialogue a dash is often written at the start of each line."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Commas",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "As in English, **no** comma goes before *que* (that), *qui, quand, si* in the middle of a sentence: *Je pense que tu as raison.* A comma does follow an introductory phrase: *Demain, je pars.*"
            },
            {
              "type": "tip",
              "en": "The app ignores punctuation when checking. Watch the space before ? and ! yourself."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Examples",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "examples",
              "items": [
                {
                  "fr": "Tu viens ce soir ?",
                  "en": "Are you coming tonight?"
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Quelle belle journée !",
                  "en": "What a lovely day!"
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Il y a trois choses : un stylo, un livre et une gomme.",
                  "en": "There are three things: a pen, a book and a rubber."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Je sais qu'il est là.",
                  "en": "I know he's here."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "id": "g-punctuation-01",
